# CopilotState Refactoring Plan

## Vision and Objective
Your vision is to create a perfectly symmetrical interface architecture for the [Autopilot](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#9-339) orchestrator:
*   **CopilotData**: Handles business data reading/writing recursively over [DataSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/data_set.dart#2-34).
*   **CopilotState**: Replaces [CopilotUX](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_ux.dart#4-25). It specifically manages transient UI state (chrome, screens, components) by proxying all operations to [StateSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#1-117).

Both [DataSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/data_set.dart#2-34) and [StateSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#1-117) belong to [Autopilot](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#9-339). The [Copilot](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_ux.dart#4-25) classes are merely specialized facades you instantiate to interact cleanly with them.

---

## Step-by-Step Execution

### Step 1: File and Class Renaming
*   Rename [lib/core/agent/copilot_ux.dart](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_ux.dart) to `lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart`.
*   Inside the new file, rename the class [CopilotUX](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_ux.dart#4-25) to `CopilotState`.

### Step 2: Expand `CopilotState` API
The current [CopilotUX](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_ux.dart#4-25) only exposes simple [getValue](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart#8-9) and [setValue](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_ux.dart#10-14), which misses the 3-tier capability embedded in [StateSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#1-117). 
I will expand `CopilotState` to explicitly provide operations for all three state granularities:
1.  **Chrome**: `getChrome(key)`, [setChrome(key, value)](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#13-20), [clearChrome()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#91-94)
2.  **Paper**: [getPaper(scope, key)](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#35-40), [setPaper(scope, key, value)](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#41-52), [clearPaper(scope)](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#83-86)
3.  **Template**: [getTemplate(scope, key)](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#59-64), [setTemplate(scope, key, value)](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#65-76), [clearTemplate(scope)](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#87-90)

### Step 3: Verify and Align [CopilotData](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart#4-25)
*   Open [lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart).
*   Ensure it cleanly handles array/object mapping over [DataSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/data_set.dart#2-34). 
*   Confirm it uses `autopilot.publishChange()` correctly.

### Step 4: Documentation Update
*   Update [docs/project_deep_analysis.md](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/docs/project_deep_analysis.md) to change all references of [CopilotUX](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_ux.dart#4-25) / [copilot_ux.dart](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_ux.dart) to `CopilotState` / `copilot_state.dart`. 
*   Adjust architectural diagrams to reflect the symmetry between [CopilotData](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart#4-25) -> [DataSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/data_set.dart#2-34) and `CopilotState` -> [StateSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#1-117).

---

## Why this is safe
Currently, [CopilotUX](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_ux.dart#4-25) and [CopilotData](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart#4-25) act as standalone definition classes in our `lib` directory and are not strongly coupled or instantiated deep within the widget tree. Therefore, this rename and structural expansion carries **zero risk** of breaking the active runtime.

Is this plan aligned with your expectations? I am ready to execute the steps when you approve.
